Now we move to the **KigaliFleet Superadmin — the control center for the entire SaaS platform.**

This is different from the company dashboard.

- **Company owner:** Manages one transport business.
- **Company employee:** Performs assigned business operations.
- **Superadmin:** Manages the entire KigaliFleet platform, all registered businesses, platform users, subscriptions, payments, system configuration, security, support and platform performance.

The Superadmin should be able to understand what is happening across KigaliFleet, investigate problems, manage platform access and protect the system.

# KigaliFleet — Superadmin Product Requirements Document

Platform administration · Version 1.0 · 9 November 2026

(Target product specification)

**Important:** This is the proposed target specification. It does not mean the current Superadmin already has these features. We must inspect the existing implementation before deciding what to change.

\# KigaliFleet — Superadmin Product Requirements Document\
\
\## 1. Product definition\
\
The Superadmin is the highest-level administrative interface for KigaliFleet.\
\
It is used by the platform owner and authorized platform administrators to manage the SaaS business and its infrastructure.\
\
The Superadmin should provide control over:\
\
\- Registered companies.\
\- Platform users.\
\- Company subscriptions.\
\- Platform revenue.\
\- Payments and billing.\
\- Platform-wide bookings and activity.\
\- Customer and company support.\
\- Platform configuration.\
\- Security and access.\
\- Notifications.\
\- System health.\
\- Integrations.\
\- Reports and analytics.\
\- Platform policies.\
\- Administrative activity.\
\
The Superadmin must not be treated as an ordinary company dashboard with more menu items.\
\
It is the control center for the entire SaaS platform.\
\
\## 2. Superadmin users and roles\
\
Not everyone working for KigaliFleet should have unrestricted access.\
\
\### A. Platform owner\
\
The highest level of platform control.\
\
Can:\
\- View platform-wide information.\
\- Manage platform administrators.\
\- Manage companies.\
\- Manage subscriptions and plans.\
\- View platform financial information.\
\- Configure platform settings.\
\- Manage integrations.\
\- Review security and audit logs.\
\- Manage platform policies.\
\- Access all authorized administration functions.\
\
\### B. Platform administrator\
\
Responsible for daily platform administration.\
\
Can:\
\- Review companies.\
\- Manage platform users.\
\- Handle approved account actions.\
\- Monitor platform activity.\
\- Handle support escalations.\
\- Review reports.\
\
Access must be restricted by assigned permissions.\
\
\### C. Finance administrator\
\
Responsible for platform financial operations.\
\
Can:\
\- View subscription payments.\
\- Track invoices.\
\- Monitor outstanding balances.\
\- Manage refunds according to authorization.\
\- Review platform revenue.\
\- Export financial reports.\
\
\### D. Customer support administrator\
\
Responsible for company and customer support.\
\
Can:\
\- View support tickets.\
\- Communicate with users.\
\- Investigate reported problems.\
\- Escalate technical issues.\
\- Review permitted company account information.\
\
Should not automatically access confidential financial or security information.\
\
\### E. Technical administrator\
\
Responsible for technical operations.\
\
Can:\
\- Monitor application health.\
\- Review system errors.\
\- Monitor integrations.\
\- Investigate failed background jobs.\
\- Review deployment and service status, where integrated.\
\- Manage approved technical configuration.\
\
\### F. Security administrator\
\
Responsible for security oversight.\
\
Can:\
\- Review suspicious activity.\
\- Investigate login events.\
\- Review access violations.\
\- Manage security incidents.\
\- Disable compromised accounts through controlled procedures.\
\
\### Role principle\
\
Every administrative role must have explicitly assigned permissions.\
\
The platform owner should be able to define who can:\
\
\- View.\
\- Create.\
\- Edit.\
\- Approve.\
\- Suspend.\
\- Delete.\
\- Export.\
\- Configure.\
\
Sensitive actions should require additional authorization and an audit record.\
\
